<h1 class="page-title">Mutli-Disciplinary Project</h1>

<p>
    <br> Contributed to a multidisciplinary climate adaptation study for Ricanau Mofo, Suriname, developing practical strategies to reduce erosion and water-related damage. The project combined nature-based solutions, riverbank protection, flood-resilient urban planning, and funding strategies to improve long-term resilience while respecting local cultural and economic constraints. The resulting framework and prototype interventions provide a scalable approach for climate adaptation in vulnerable river communities.
    
    Please find the report <strong><a href="https://repository.tudelft.nl/record/uuid:3fa2160c-f2e2-4f81-90d8-9a6f56f856ed" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">here</a></strong>.
</p>

